    "primary_DOI": "10.1093/gpbjnl/qzag027",
    "license": "CC-BY-4.0",
    "access": "Open public author expression archive; no preview token, controlled WGS data or own genotype inference used.",
    "source_sample_review": {
      "path": "references/datasets/PRJEB86440_source_identity_review.json",
      "bytes": 21046,
      "sha256": "174218714122a5926afd3bf8707c26742ef90b1b96d2b978d891c626470f2d9d"
    },
    "source_unit": "Sixty-two study-scoped coded sample/material groups, one retained capture view per explicit csp_code_n. The source data guide documents patient-ID matching via supplementary S1 and deposited sample/WGS aliases. Twelve unpooled rows share a no-WGS-needed placeholder; it is not a participant alias. Resequenced suffixes are explicitly linked by csp_code_n and do not add people. Counts represent study-coded groups, not globally verified independent participants.",
    "identity_policy": "Original annotation pair selects pooled capture, explicit csp_code_n selects unpooled capture; literal original barcode selects count row. Deposited author sample aliases join supplementary WGS names and .best SNG.1ST calls with only an explicit optional_L00 suffix. No SNP/profile/genotype inference or ordinal donor assignment. Exact per-cell source/call disagreements excluded; every coded sample remains represented.",
    "clinical_policy": "Supplementary S1 provides source-coded condition, age, sex, institution, diagnosis age and disease duration. Keep literal source labels/units and original annotated short_stat/institution fields; institution uses different coding in the two sources. No exact clinical clock, medication, blood-draw date, family-pair or cross-study alias imputation. Relatives create potential family dependence; family links are unresolved and splits remain unassigned.",
    "reuse_policy": "No completed source accession/Zenodo record/PMID/DOI reuse reference found. All40captures belong to one study; 28pooled and12unpooled files are not40participants. Source62coded clinical rows are not extra independent samples per capture/modality. Global aliases and family groups remain unresolved.",
    "selection_policy": "Native bundle retains all325581exact originalcount-matched authorcells and all36601provided RNAaxes. Processing must exclude source_assignment_eligible=False (author nonsinglet and unresolved/deposited nonsinglet demuxcalls);309564source-assignment/author-singlet/RNAQCcells remain.273absent sourcebarcodes remain outside bundle, with originalmetadata/RNAquantityNaNs retained in sourceproof. No gene/profile/cell identity reconstruction.",
    "cell_calling_policy": "Original Cell Ranger count matrices and deposited author selected cells; preserve conflicting doublet labels. Require source_assignment_eligible=True (explicit original source assignment and author singlet) plus fixed native-RNA QC. Native axes include all36601provided genes; transformed X/raw.X, selected3000gene counts, integrated latents and source feature-selection statistics do not define geometry.",
    "count_version_policy": "Five original capture matrices disagreewith authorcachedQC on all42738matchedrows; preserve actual deposited count vectors and explicit per-cell versionflag. Other captures agree. Do not alter counts to fit cachedvalues. Causeunresolved; stratify or exclude flagged captures in sensitivity analysis.",
    "gene_policy": "All36601provided GRCh38geneIDs with originalsymbols;10duplicate symbols remain distinct native axes, summedonly for fixed-reference annotation.",
    "count_semantics": "Every953804319stored original Cell Ranger RNA count value finite/nonnegative/integer. All36601sourcegeneIDs retained. Five capture count versions disagree with cached author RNAQC; use deposited counts without forcing cached equality.",
    "source_limitations": "Study-coded sample/material groups and donor-code groups do not establish globally unique independent participants. First-degree family dependence lacks an explicit family crosswalk. Five count-release/cached-QC discrepancies,273absent rawbarcodes and conflicting author/original doublet calls are retained. Primary full-methods HTTP403; source data guide/clinical table/cell assignments provide direct processing evidence. Individual exactclinical clocks/medication/globalaliases unassigned."
  }
